   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the highway law, in relation to designating a portion of the\nstate highway system as the \"Peter Wheeler Memorial Bridge\"",
    "basePrintNo": "S4262",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4262-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §344-p, Hway L",
    "lawSection": "Highway Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S4262\n\nSPONSOR: WEBB\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the highway law, in relation to designating a portion of\nthe state highway system as the \"Peter Wheeler Memorial Bridge\"\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nDesignates a bridge on the state highway system in Lansing, NY as the\n\"Peter Wheeler Memorial Bridge\"\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 adds new section 344-o to the Highway Law to require that a\nportion of the state highway system be designated as the \"Peter Wheeler\nMemorial Bridge\".\n\nSection 2 requires the commissioner of transportation to provide for the\ninstallation and maintenance of adequate signing of the state highway\nsystem as designated pursuant to section one of this act.\n\nSection 3 provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Town of Lansing wishes to honor Peter Wheeler, a slave that once\nlived in Ludlowville in the early 1800s, by designating the newly\nconstructed bridge crossing Salmon Creek as the \"Peter Wheeler Memorial\nBridge.\" The community believes it is not only important to remember the\nstory of Wheeler, but it is also important to remember the dark history\nof slavery in the community. While Peter Wheeler was not the only slave\nin Tompkins County, there is an extensive narrative of what his life was\nlike as a slave in Ludlowville, New York.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
